{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14270561,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":2,"pointsAwarded":2,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57964,"firstName":"William","lastName":"Parker","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO2MGD4gcTFRx970s7DzjQk","sequenceId":15},"course":{"id":76,"name":"Methods of Proof"},"topic":{"id":248,"name":"Biconditional Statements"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T16:47:18.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T17:20:25.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T17:22:08.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T17:22:21.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62396052,"created":"2026-10-16T17:20:38.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12750,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 5:20 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":83223,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12715,"text":"<p>\\[\n(P \\lor Q) \\Leftrightarrow Q \\, \\equiv \\, \\bbox[3pt, white, border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAAAAAAA}} \\land  \\big[Q \\Rightarrow (P\\lor Q)\\big]\n\\]</p>\n<p>What expression should be inserted into the blank space above to give logically equivalent statements?</p>\n","choice1":"$(P\\lor Q) \\Rightarrow Q $","choice2":"$Q \\Rightarrow (P\\lor Q)$","choice3":"$Q \\Rightarrow P$","choice4":"$P \\Rightarrow Q$","choice5":"$  P \\lor Q   $","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>According to the definition of the biconditional, </p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$A \\Leftrightarrow B$ is true if $A\\Rightarrow B$ <strong>and</strong> $B\\Rightarrow A.$ Otherwise, it is false.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>In other words, $A \\Leftrightarrow B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So in this case, we have\n\\[\n(P\\lor Q) \\Leftrightarrow Q \\equiv \\big[\\,\\bbox[2pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}(P\\lor Q) \\Rightarrow Q}\\big] \\land \\big[Q \\Rightarrow (P\\lor Q)\\big].\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore, the missing part is $(P\\lor Q) \\Rightarrow Q.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":248,"name":"Biconditional Statements"},"example":{"id":12715,"title":"Writing Biconditionals as Conditionals"},"group":{"id":24502,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14270561,"answer":{"id":62396052,"cread":"2026-10-16T17:20:38.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12750},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62396064,"created":"2026-10-16T17:20:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10050,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 5:20 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":83228,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":12718,"text":"<p>$\\lnot (A \\Leftrightarrow \\neg B) \\equiv $</p>\n","choice1":"$(A \\land B) \\lor (\\neg B \\land \\neg A)$","choice2":"$\\neg A \\Leftrightarrow B$","choice3":"$(\\neg A \\land B) \\land (\\neg B \\lor \\neg A)$","choice4":"$\\neg (A \\land \\neg B) \\lor B$","choice5":"$(A \\land B) \\Rightarrow (\\neg B \\land A)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we use the definition of the biconditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: </p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\lnot (A \\Leftrightarrow \\lnot B) \n\t\t\\equiv \\lnot \\big[(A \\Rightarrow \\lnot B) \\land (\\lnot B \\Rightarrow A)\\big]\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\lnot \\big[(A \\Rightarrow \\lnot B) \\land (\\lnot B \\Rightarrow A)\\big] \n\t\t\\equiv \\lnot \\big[(\\lnot A \\lor \\lnot B) \\land (\\lnot\\lnot B \\lor A)\\big] \n\\]</p>\n<p>Next, we use De Morgan&#39;s laws:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\t \\lnot \\big[(\\neg A \\lor \\neg B) \\land (\\lnot\\lnot B \\lor A)\\big]\n\t\t&\\equiv \\lnot (\\neg A \\lor \\lnot B) \\lor \\lnot (\\lnot\\lnot B \\lor A) \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&\\equiv (\\lnot\\lnot A \\land \\lnot\\lnot B) \\lor (\\lnot\\lnot\\lnot B \\land \\lnot A)\t\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Finally, we simplify the double negations:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t (\\lnot\\lnot A \\land \\lnot\\lnot B) \\lor (\\lnot\\lnot\\lnot B \\land \\lnot A)\n\t\t\t\\equiv  (A \\land B) \\lor (\\lnot B \\land \\lnot A) \n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":248,"name":"Biconditional Statements"},"example":{"id":12718,"title":"Simplifying Expressions Involving Equivalences"},"group":{"id":24505,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14270561,"answer":{"id":62396064,"cread":"2026-10-16T17:20:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10050},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62396082,"created":"2026-10-16T17:21:08.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12557,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 5:21 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":182518,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12715,"text":"<p>$\nP \\Leftrightarrow \\neg Q \\equiv \n$</p>\n","choice1":"$(P \\Rightarrow \\neg Q) \\land ( \\neg Q \\Rightarrow P)$","choice2":"$(P \\Rightarrow \\neg Q) \\lor ( \\neg Q \\Rightarrow P)$","choice3":"$P\\Rightarrow \\neg Q $","choice4":"$(P \\Rightarrow Q) \\lor (Q \\Rightarrow P)$","choice5":"$(P \\Rightarrow Q) \\land (Q \\Rightarrow P)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>According to the definition of the biconditional, </p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$A \\Leftrightarrow B$ is true if $A\\Rightarrow B$ <strong>and</strong> $B\\Rightarrow A.$ Otherwise, it is false.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>In other words, $A \\Leftrighta